# 回答例：入力を検証し、更新を一つの原子的操作へ渡す

## Java：2つのTODOメソッドだけを置換する

```java
public static int validId(String raw) {
    if (raw == null || !raw.matches("[0-9]+")) throw new IllegalArgumentException("invalid id");
    try {
        int id = Integer.parseInt(raw);
        if (id <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("invalid id");
        return id;
    } catch (NumberFormatException error) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("invalid id");
    }
}

public Update rename(String raw, String title, int expectedVersion) {
    int id = validId(raw);
    if (title == null || title.matches("[ \\t\\r\\n]*") || expectedVersion < 1)
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("invalid update");
    return repository.compareAndSet(id, title, expectedVersion);
}
```

数字の判定だけでなく、変換時の範囲も検査する。NumberFormatExceptionはIllegalArgumentExceptionの派生なので、外側へ統一した型で返す。入力不正と未登録は分ける。取得したBookのversionを調べてから無条件更新しても、実DBでは競合を防げない。

## Rust：2つのTODO関数だけを置換する

```rust
pub fn valid_id(raw: &str) -> Result<i32, &'static str> {
    if raw.is_empty() || !raw.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_digit()) { return Err("invalid id"); }
    raw.parse::<i32>().ok().filter(|id| *id > 0).ok_or("invalid id")
}

pub fn rename(repository: &mut Repository, raw: &str, title: &str, expected: i32) -> Result<Update, &'static str> {
    let id = valid_id(raw)?;
    if title.chars().all(|c| matches!(c, ' ' | '\t' | '\r' | '\n')) || expected < 1 {
        return Err("invalid update");
    }
    Ok(repository.compare_and_set(id, title, expected))
}
```

`?`で入力不正を呼び出し側へ返す。Optionの未登録とResultの入力不正を混同しない。排他的な借用はこのモデルでの同時アクセスを制約するが、分散システムの排他やDBトランザクションを自動で実装するものではない。

## テスト設計をさらに良くする

- 先頭0と最大値を受け入れるか確認する。
- 成功だけでなく、競合・不正入力の後にデータが変化しないことを確認する。
- 更新の成功は既存版との比較を含む操作にする。別SELECTの判定だけで済ませない。
- 実DBでは更新件数・トランザクション・障害時のrollbackを別に試す。
- この小さな教材のversionはi32/int。最大値に達する運用やIDの重複登録、認証、HTTP入力の最大長等は未実装であり、実サービスにそのまま持ち込まない。

import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.Optional;

/** Teaching starter: implement the two TODOs, then run WorkplaceTest. */
public final class BookService {
    public record Book(int id, String title, int version) {}
    public enum Update { UPDATED, MISSING, CONFLICT }
    public interface Repository {
        Optional<Book> find(int id);
        Update compareAndSet(int id, String title, int expectedVersion);
    }
    public static final class MemoryRepository implements Repository {
        private final Map<Integer, Book> books = new HashMap<>();
        public MemoryRepository() { books.put(1, new Book(1, "Java", 1)); }
        public synchronized Optional<Book> find(int id) { return Optional.ofNullable(books.get(id)); }
        public synchronized Update compareAndSet(int id, String title, int expectedVersion) {
            Book old = books.get(id);
            if (old == null) return Update.MISSING;
            if (old.version() != expectedVersion) return Update.CONFLICT;
            books.put(id, new Book(id, title, old.version() + 1));
            return Update.UPDATED;
        }
    }
    private final Repository repository;
    public BookService(Repository repository) { this.repository = repository; }

    public static int validId(String raw) {
        // TODO 1: ASCII digits only; leading zero allowed; 1..2147483647.
        // Reject null/empty/invalid/range error with IllegalArgumentException.
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException("TODO validId");
    }
    public Optional<Book> find(String raw) { return repository.find(validId(raw)); }

    public Update rename(String raw, String title, int expectedVersion) {
        // TODO 2: validate id/title/version, then call the atomic repository operation.
        // Do NOT implement read -> check -> unconditional write in this layer.
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException("TODO rename");
    }
}

import java.util.Optional;

public final class WorkplaceTest {
    private static int passed, failed;
    private static void check(boolean condition) { if (!condition) throw new AssertionError("expectation mismatch"); }
    private static void rejects(Runnable action) {
        try { action.run(); } catch (IllegalArgumentException expected) { return; }
        throw new AssertionError("expected IllegalArgumentException");
    }
    private static void test(String name, Runnable body) {
        try { body.run(); passed++; System.out.println("PASS " + name); }
        catch (Throwable error) { failed++; System.out.println("FAIL " + name + ": " + error); }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        test("valid IDs and leading zeros", () -> {
            check(BookService.validId("1") == 1);
            check(BookService.validId("001") == 1);
            check(BookService.validId("2147483647") == Integer.MAX_VALUE);
        });
        test("strict format and range", () -> {
            for (String raw : new String[]{null,"","0","-1","+1","1abc","１","1.0"," 1","2147483648"}) rejects(() -> BookService.validId(raw));
        });
        test("invalid ID never calls repository", () -> {
            BookService.Repository trap = new BookService.Repository() {
                public Optional<BookService.Book> find(int id) { throw new AssertionError("repository reached"); }
                public BookService.Update compareAndSet(int id, String title, int version) { throw new AssertionError("repository reached"); }
            };
            rejects(() -> new BookService(trap).find("abc"));
            rejects(() -> new BookService(trap).rename("abc", "name", 1));
            rejects(() -> new BookService(trap).rename("1", "", 1));
            rejects(() -> new BookService(trap).rename("1", "name", 0));
        });
        test("found and missing remain distinct", () -> {
            BookService service = new BookService(new BookService.MemoryRepository());
            check(service.find("1").orElseThrow().title().equals("Java"));
            check(service.find("2").isEmpty());
        });
        test("successful rename increments version", () -> {
            BookService service = new BookService(new BookService.MemoryRepository());
            check(service.rename("1", "Java実践", 1) == BookService.Update.UPDATED);
            check(service.find("1").orElseThrow().equals(new BookService.Book(1, "Java実践", 2)));
        });
        test("two readers cannot silently overwrite", () -> {
            BookService service = new BookService(new BookService.MemoryRepository());
            int a = service.find("1").orElseThrow().version();
            int b = service.find("1").orElseThrow().version();
            check(service.rename("1", "Aの変更", a) == BookService.Update.UPDATED);
            check(service.rename("1", "Bの変更", b) == BookService.Update.CONFLICT);
            check(service.find("1").orElseThrow().equals(new BookService.Book(1, "Aの変更", 2)));
        });
        test("missing update changes nothing", () -> {
            BookService service = new BookService(new BookService.MemoryRepository());
            check(service.rename("2", "存在しない本", 1) == BookService.Update.MISSING);
            check(service.find("1").orElseThrow().version() == 1);
        });
        test("invalid title and version change nothing", () -> {
            BookService service = new BookService(new BookService.MemoryRepository());
            for (String title : new String[]{null,""," \t\r\n"}) rejects(() -> service.rename("1", title, 1));
            rejects(() -> service.rename("1", "有効な名前", 0));
            check(service.find("1").orElseThrow().equals(new BookService.Book(1, "Java", 1)));
        });
        System.out.println(passed + " passed, " + failed + " failed");
        if (failed != 0) throw new AssertionError("Complete the TODOs and rerun the tests.");
    }
}

use std::collections::HashMap;

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Book { pub id: i32, pub title: String, pub version: i32 }
#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Update { Updated, Missing, Conflict }
pub struct Repository { books: HashMap<i32, Book> }
impl Default for Repository {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self { books: HashMap::from([(1, Book { id: 1, title: "Rust".into(), version: 1 })]) }
    }
}
impl Repository {
    pub fn find(&self, id: i32) -> Option<Book> { self.books.get(&id).cloned() }
    // The exclusive &mut borrow keeps comparison and mutation together in this model.
    pub fn compare_and_set(&mut self, id: i32, title: &str, expected: i32) -> Update {
        let Some(book) = self.books.get_mut(&id) else { return Update::Missing; };
        if book.version != expected { return Update::Conflict; }
        book.title = title.to_owned();
        book.version += 1;
        Update::Updated
    }
}
pub fn valid_id(_raw: &str) -> Result<i32, &'static str> {
    // TODO 1: ASCII digits only, leading zero allowed, 1..2147483647.
    todo!("valid_id")
}
pub fn find(repository: &Repository, raw: &str) -> Result<Option<Book>, &'static str> {
    Ok(repository.find(valid_id(raw)?))
}
